contributors as stated in that package.

What was taken
--------------
Only the pure parse path used by here.build's TUI diff projection:

  - dist/utils/parseDiffFromFile.js
  - dist/utils/parsePatchFiles.js
  - dist/utils/cleanLastNewline.js
  - dist/utils/detachString.js
  - related constants from dist/constants.js

Not taken: React/DOM components (CodeView, FileDiff, …), SSR, workers,
highlighters, CSS, or any code that touches `navigator` / the DOM.

Why
---
The published package entry re-exports browser UI that evaluates
`navigator.userAgent` at module load time, which crashes under Node (storybook
fixtures, tests, harness CLI). We only need structured hunk metadata.

Modifications by here.build
---------------------------
  - TypeScript modules and local type definitions for the parse surface
  - Dropped unused constants / exports
  - No intentional changes to parse algorithms

